From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a profile loads none of Chrome's AI component
 extensions

The field trial testing config turns on `Glic` (study GlicDogfood) and
`ApiContextualTasksPrivate` (study ContextualTasksRearchitecture), so
ComponentLoader::AddGlicExtension and AddContextualTasksExtension loaded
Gemini in Chrome's and Contextual Tasks' extensions into every profile.
Each one's service worker runs in a renderer of its own, about 30 MiB, at
startup and again whenever a page opens. A desk has neither feature's UI.
An Electron app's window woke them in both the desk's profiles, which is
why the app cost more on the engine than on its own Electron in the
`electron-app-on-a-tty` VM check.

Both now add nothing.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`. Guarded by guard-no-chrome-component-extensions.
---
 chrome/browser/extensions/component_loader.cc | 24 ++++++++----------------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/extensions/component_loader.cc b/chrome/browser/extensions/component_loader.cc
index e88059b..241811f 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/component_loader.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/component_loader.cc
@@ -586,22 +586,14 @@ void ComponentLoader::AddNewTabPageExtension() {
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_WEBUI_NTP)
 }
 
-void ComponentLoader::AddGlicExtension() {
-  if (IsApiGlicPrivateEnabled()) {
-    Add(IDR_GLIC_EXTENSION_MANIFEST,
-        base::FilePath(FILE_PATH_LITERAL("glic_extension")));
-  }
-}
-
-void ComponentLoader::AddContextualTasksExtension() {
-  if (base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(
-          extensions_features::kApiContextualTasksPrivate) ||
-      base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(
-          extensions_features::kApiContextualTasksPrivateAba)) {
-    Add(IDR_CONTEXTUAL_TASKS_EXTENSION_MANIFEST_JSON,
-        base::FilePath(FILE_PATH_LITERAL("contextual_tasks_extension")));
-  }
-}
+// Domicile's engine fork: a desk has no Gemini in Chrome and no contextual
+// tasks side panel, so neither of their component extensions loads. The field
+// trial testing config turns on the features that load them, and then each
+// one's service worker starts a renderer in every profile, about 30 MiB each,
+// whenever a page opens.
+void ComponentLoader::AddGlicExtension() {}
+
+void ComponentLoader::AddContextualTasksExtension() {}
 
 void ComponentLoader::AddWithNameAndDescription(
     int manifest_resource_id,
